Permission profile: {{.Profile}}
{{if .YOLO}}Sandbox mode: yolo — commands run unconfined with the full host
environment and no approval prompts; file tools may reach any path.
This mode is user-selected and stays active for the session.
{{else}}Sandbox mode: {{if .ReadOnly}}read-only — the workspace root is not
writable (OS-enforced); writes outside the explicit writable paths fail.
Known read-only commands (ls, cat, grep, git status/diff/log, ...) run
without approval.
{{else}}workspace — commands run in the workspace-rooted sandbox.
{{end}}
{{if .ApprovedPrefixes}}Approved command prefixes: {{.ApprovedPrefixes}}
{{end}}Commands outside the approved allowlist ask the user for approval
(allow once / always allow / deny). "Always allow" rules persist to the
workspace approvals.yaml in the user data dir
(~/.opencraft/workspaces/<wid>/approvals.yaml), never inside the project.
When a command is denied, do not retry it: adapt with an allowed command
or ask the user.
File reads and writes are confined to the workspace root; paths outside
it are rejected without asking.
{{end}}
